  "note_on_ridge_preprocessing": "Ridge in the main experiments (phase2_pipeline.py, phase4_multimodel_multipartition.py) is fit on raw, unstandardized Magpie features with alpha=1.0. Magpie features span very different raw scales (e.g. AtomicWeight ~1-250, Electronegativity ~0.7-4, valence counts ~0-18), so a single fixed alpha gives uneven effective regularization across features (the effective ridge penalty scales with 1/variance of the feature in its raw units). This is a second contributor to the instability of Ridge, separate from the eigenstructure mechanism tested above; standardizing features before Ridge or ElasticNet addresses it.",
  "verdict": "Across the 5 worst- and 5 best-performing Ridge family-disjoint partitions, the theory-motivated weighted projection of the held-out family's mean feature deviation onto the training covariance's low-eigenvalue (under-constrained) subspace is modestly larger for the worst partitions (worst5 mean=7.941e+04 vs. best5 mean=4.820e+04), and the pearson correlation across all 10 partitions is r=-0.137 (p=0.706). An earlier, simpler (unweighted) Mahalanobis-distance test did not hold after controlling for test-set size; this eigenvalue-weighted projection is a separate test motivated by ridge regression theory."
